From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:26:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/30] swgl: build the feature level 9_3 pixel shaders and the
 glue that feeds them

For Windows targets, swgl's build script now translates each program's
fragment half with glsl-to-cxx's HLSL back end and compiles it with fxc
(ps_4_0_level_9_3). The bytecode goes into <shader>_gpu.h. glsl-to-cxx
gives every program class three GPU hooks:
- gpu_info(): the bytecode and its varying layout, or null;
- gpu_pack(): after the vertex shader has run a quad, copies its
  interpolated outputs and the program's flat fields into the packed
  per-vertex layout and the flat-texture run;
- gpu_sampler_unit(): the texture unit behind each sampler.

gpu_shaders.h carries the eight pass-through vertex shaders (one per count
of texture coordinates) and a clear shader. They flip Y so that memory row
0 stays GL's row 0, as in SWGL's own buffers, and map depth to [0, 1].

Of the 39 programs, 33 get a GPU pixel shader. The rest stay on the CPU:
the blurs, the gradient and the SVG filter exceed the 512 instructions of
ps_2_x, and two glyph-transform text variants use gl_ClipDistance. Nothing
calls the hooks yet. SWGL_FXC overrides where fxc comes from; set it empty
to leave the GPU path out.

Wrench gets a GeckoW10mNote that prints to stderr, since WebRender on this
port calls it and wrench has no xul. Wrench builds and links again on
Windows with clang-cl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
